dentity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"banned","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"banned","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"banned","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"banned","vintage":"restricted"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}","name":"Sol Ring","oracle_id":"6ad8011d-3471-4369-9d68-b264cc027487","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}{C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Twiddle","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","oracle_text":"You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2003-07-28","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Clue is an artifact type. Even though it appears on some cards with other permanent types, it's never a creature type, a land type, or anything but an artifact type.","oracle_id":"10d8f29a-d483-4f06-bc13-d41d62847ffe","published_at":"2024-02-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Senator Peacock somehow becomes an artifact, it will also be a Clue.","oracle_id":"10d8f29a-d483-4f06-bc13-d41d62847ffe","published_at":"2024-02-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect refers to a Clue, it means any Clue artifact, not just a Clue artifact token. For example, you can sacrifice Wrench to pay for Alquist Proft, Master Sleuth's activated ability.","oracle_id":"10d8f29a-d483-4f06-bc13-d41d62847ffe","published_at":"2024-02-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some abilities trigger \"whenever you sacrifice a Clue\". Those abilities trigger whenever you sacrifice a Clue for any reason, not just to activate a Clue's activated ability.","oracle_id":"10d8f29a-d483-4f06-bc13-d41d62847ffe","published_at":"2024-02-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some spells and abilities that investigate may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve. You won't create any Clue tokens.","oracle_id":"10d8f29a-d483-4f06-bc13-d41d62847ffe","published_at":"2024-02-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The artifacts retain any types, subtypes, supertypes, and abilities they have.","oracle_id":"10d8f29a-d483-4f06-bc13-d41d62847ffe","published_at":"2024-02-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can't sacrifice a Clue to pay multiple costs. For example, you can't sacrifice a Clue token to activate its own ability and also to activate Alquist Proft, Master Sleuth's ability.","oracle_id":"10d8f29a-d483-4f06-bc13-d41d62847ffe","published_at":"2024-02-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The triggered ability Mephidross Vampire grants to each creature you control triggers on any damage dealt to any creature, not just combat damage.","oracle_id":"a6763205-47c7-4d7f-be8c-2f69e8321048","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"With a Humility and two Opalescences on the battlefield, if Humility has the latest timestamp, then all creatures are 1/1 with no abilities. If the timestamp order is Opalescence, Humility, Opalescence, the second Opalescence is 1/1, and the Humility and first Opalescence are 4/4. If Humility has the earliest timestamp, then everything is 4/4.","oracle_id":"ed7bdb3e-5c51-4547-9266-76a791e0b2b0","published_at":"2006-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Removes all creature abilities. This includes mana abilities. Animated lands will also lose the ability to tap for mana.","oracle_id":"ed7bdb3e-5c51-4547-9266-76a791e0b2b0","published_at":"2007-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is the current interaction between Humility and Opalescence:\u00a0The type-changing effect applies at layer 4, but the rest happens in the applicable layers. The rest of it will apply even if the permanent loses its ability before it's finished applying. So if Opalescence, Humility, and Worship are on the battlefield and Opalescence entered before Humility, the following is true: Layer 4: Humility and Worship each become creatures that are still enchantments. (Opalescence). Layer 6: Humility and Worship each lose their abilities. (Humility) Layer 7b: Humility becomes 4/4 and Worship becomes 4/4. (Opalescence). Humility becomes 1/1 and Worship becomes 1/1 (Humility). But if Humility entered before Opalescence, the following is true: Layer 4: Humility and Worship each become creatures that are still enchantments (Opalescence). Layer 6: Humility and Worship each lose their abilities (Humility). Layer 7b: Humility becomes 1/1 and Worship becomes 1/1 (Humility). Humility becomes 4/4 and Worship becomes 4/4 (Opalescence).","oracle_id":"ed7bdb3e-5c51-4547-9266-76a791e0b2b0","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Becoming an artifact doesn't change what color(s) a permanent is.","oracle_id":"f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may target any permanent with the ability, including an artifact.","oracle_id":"f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
